# E1: the EXACTNESS CONTROL, UNAUDITED: c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost-log (the traffic profile plus the ledger flag and nothing else, so its engine path is the traffic profile's byte for byte) on the same image as E2.
# Audits are off on purpose: the audited eight-seat profiles cost about 8.4 minutes a request. The tests are the shapes that exercise every path a lever touches: the four-live round (one block, one quad), the eight-live
# round (two blocks, two quads), eight same-length code users, eight 32k code users, the resend, the non-streamed replays (the sequential step), the split block and the drain (admissions and detaches: the keyed write's full, diff and padded rounds).
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean, every answer completes, no stall; RECORD every test's per-user content hash, reasoning hash, completion tokens and finish reason (the smoke JSON) and the position-keyed [PACKED] lines: E2 must equal them. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/round-host window (docs/tp4-round-host.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/round-host and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph and every read rule.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/round-host commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost-log
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code_32k,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,replay_concurrent8,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
